WEBVTT

00:08.530 --> 00:10.570
[ERWIN]
Let's move!

00:19.880 --> 00:22.450
[HANGE grunts]

00:22.480 --> 00:23.810
Hange?

00:23.850 --> 00:26.320
Get, get me a horse.

00:26.350 --> 00:29.650
Section Commander!
Where're you going?

00:29.690 --> 00:31.190
Back to the village
where we caught

00:31.220 --> 00:33.320
the Titan that couldn't walk.

00:33.360 --> 00:34.990
Not Ragako!

00:35.030 --> 00:37.390
I need to see.

00:37.460 --> 00:39.530
Have you lost touch
with reality?

00:39.570 --> 00:43.530
You're in no condition
to ride horseback right now!

00:44.800 --> 00:46.570
There's something
important there.

00:46.640 --> 00:49.010
I feel it in my bones.

00:51.440 --> 00:54.510
All right, fine.

00:54.550 --> 00:55.980
I'll go myself.

00:56.010 --> 00:59.050
You stay here
and quit trying to move!

01:04.390 --> 01:08.230
Be on the lookout!
All riders assume formation!

01:18.240 --> 01:20.000
[MIKASA]
Eren.

01:20.570 --> 01:25.580
♪ Opening Song

02:59.150 --> 03:01.420
[REINER]
You're awake.

03:01.490 --> 03:03.360
Welcome back.

03:12.270 --> 03:14.470
[Gasps]

03:16.240 --> 03:21.740
[Breathe heavily]

03:21.780 --> 03:26.110
[Gasps]
What the hell? My arms!

03:26.180 --> 03:27.880
[YMIR]
Eren.

03:27.920 --> 03:31.280
I'm, uh, not in any
better shape here.

03:31.350 --> 03:34.090
Seems we're both
having a shit day.

03:34.120 --> 03:39.060
Ymir. What did they...
What did they do to me?

03:39.090 --> 03:44.400
[REINER] Sorry. That was...
That was my fault.

03:44.430 --> 03:46.730
You can pin
your injuries on me.

03:46.770 --> 03:49.200
Guess I was in kind of
a hurry back there.

03:49.240 --> 03:55.110
Bit your nape without
thinking about your arms.

03:55.140 --> 04:01.180
Is that right? So. I lost.

04:10.390 --> 04:12.130
Eren! Don't do it!

04:12.160 --> 04:14.590
Easy there, hothead.

04:14.630 --> 04:17.060
Take a look at where we are.

04:17.100 --> 04:20.630
This is the giant forest
within Wall Maria.

04:20.670 --> 04:24.270
Wall Rose is leagues away.

04:24.310 --> 04:26.340
Which means...
we're deep in the heart

04:26.410 --> 04:29.940
of Titan country. See?

04:29.980 --> 04:33.080
I think our buddy
down there is an abnormal.

04:33.120 --> 04:35.820
It may look like
he's just kickin' back,

04:35.850 --> 04:39.420
but those eyes
haven't left us once.

04:39.450 --> 04:41.760
Lot of smaller ones
down there, too.

04:41.790 --> 04:46.960
That's plenty bad enough.
Another big one over there.

04:47.000 --> 04:49.700
Fixated but
keeping his distance.

04:49.770 --> 04:53.330
Strikes me as the shy type.

04:53.370 --> 04:55.800
And then there are
these chumps.

04:55.840 --> 04:57.700
Dirty bastards.

04:57.770 --> 05:00.810
They had the foresight
to suit up in full gear.

05:00.840 --> 05:04.110
'Course Reiner took yours.

05:04.150 --> 05:06.210
Point is, changing into
a Titan isn't gonna

05:06.280 --> 05:08.680
accomplish very much right now.

05:08.720 --> 05:11.020
One, they can do
the same thing if they want.

05:11.050 --> 05:13.950
Two, they can zip
into the trees if not.

05:13.990 --> 05:17.390
Three, we're basically
surrounded on all sides.

05:17.460 --> 05:20.490
Power or no power, getting out
of this would be tricky as hell,

05:20.530 --> 05:24.130
even at the best of times.

05:24.170 --> 05:25.670
Y'read me?

05:25.700 --> 05:28.640
There's nothing to gain
by being a dumbass.

05:28.670 --> 05:30.540
[REINER]
She's right.

05:30.570 --> 05:33.470
Y'can't turn into Titans
right now anyway.

05:33.510 --> 05:37.080
Don't count on that ability
coming to the rescue.

05:37.150 --> 05:39.350
The body can only take so much.

05:39.380 --> 05:42.850
It's a little preoccupied
with healing at the moment.

05:44.390 --> 05:47.020
Nice try. You expect
me to sit here

05:47.060 --> 05:49.820
and take the word of liar?

05:52.830 --> 05:56.030
Yeah, well. We're sort of
at a disadvantage here.

05:56.060 --> 05:59.100
It's not like we know the ins
and outs of how this works.

05:59.170 --> 06:01.570
Unlike you guys,
I'm basically clueless

06:01.600 --> 06:03.600
about the whole thing.

06:03.670 --> 06:05.840
Hey, Reiner.

06:05.870 --> 06:09.280
You said you'd start
talking once Eren was up.

06:09.340 --> 06:11.510
Don't'cha think it's
about time somebody explains

06:11.550 --> 06:13.850
what you plan on doing with us?

06:15.620 --> 06:19.050
[REINER] We're taking you
to our hometown.

06:19.090 --> 06:23.190
Of course, I realize neither of
you is just gonna do as I ask.

06:23.230 --> 06:24.920
Like Ymir was saying, though,

06:24.960 --> 06:30.130
this place is crawling with
Titans. They're everywhere.

06:30.200 --> 06:32.030
We could beat the living
shit out of each other

06:32.070 --> 06:34.270
if that's what you want.

06:34.340 --> 06:36.300
But I wouldn't recommend it.

06:36.370 --> 06:38.170
Our friends
down below are hungry

06:38.240 --> 06:40.440
and not prone to discriminate.

06:40.480 --> 06:42.910
[REINER] Whether you try to
cut and run or stick around,

06:42.940 --> 06:46.380
believe me when I say
our options are limited.

06:46.410 --> 06:49.650
We wait for nightfall.

06:49.720 --> 06:51.480
So, why didn't you
just stay in Titan form

06:51.550 --> 06:53.090
and run all the way home?

06:53.120 --> 06:55.890
What's the point of stopping
here in the first place?

06:55.920 --> 06:59.290
You get winded
and have to take a break?

06:59.330 --> 07:02.160
Why don't you
use your imagination?

07:02.230 --> 07:04.330
[YMIR sighs]

07:05.770 --> 07:09.840
[EREN] Let me think.
Suppose I wait for an opening.

07:09.910 --> 07:12.770
If I assume Titan form,
running away wouldn't really

07:12.810 --> 07:15.410
be that much of a challenge.

07:15.440 --> 07:21.310
Question is, can I assume
Titan form in this condition?

07:21.350 --> 07:24.020
Reiner doesn't seem to think so,

07:24.090 --> 07:25.920
and it's not like he
and Bertholdt would risk

07:25.950 --> 07:29.120
stopping here
without a good reason.

07:29.160 --> 07:32.390
What if I couldn't
transform to full strength?

07:32.430 --> 07:36.030
Does that mean the other Titans
would be able to eat me?

07:37.470 --> 07:39.030
So we're just gonna
sit on our asses

07:39.100 --> 07:40.670
till the sun goes down?

07:40.700 --> 07:42.340
[REINER]
It's a possibility.

07:42.370 --> 07:46.340
[EREN] No. Why give us
the chance to recover?

07:46.370 --> 07:50.840
If they wait for nightfall
we'd only be harder to rein in.

07:50.880 --> 07:54.480
They'll make their move
while we're still helpless.

07:56.020 --> 08:01.020
At this rate I can't
do anything. We're screwed.

08:01.060 --> 08:03.020
[Gasps]

08:03.060 --> 08:05.290
What happened
to everyone else?

08:05.330 --> 08:07.630
Where are the Scouts?

08:11.470 --> 08:14.000
Don't tell me they're
coming here to save us.

08:14.040 --> 08:16.740
Oh god. If they show up,
none of 'em will--

08:16.810 --> 08:17.900
Wait a second.

08:17.970 --> 08:19.510
Those Titans at the castle
had no problem

08:19.540 --> 08:23.680
moving around at night.
What's stopping these guys?

08:23.710 --> 08:26.310
[REINER] The Titans here
can't move after dark.

08:26.350 --> 08:29.820
But then you know all
about that, don't you, Ymir?

08:33.250 --> 08:36.760
[EREN] How is it she's able
to transform into a Titan?

08:36.830 --> 08:40.360
Doesn't seem to catch her
off-guard like it did me.

08:40.400 --> 08:42.100
What's her angle?

08:42.160 --> 08:44.900
Who's side is
she on in all this?

08:44.930 --> 08:48.300
If I thought she was
hard to read before...

08:50.710 --> 08:54.440
I've made up my mind.
I need information.

08:54.510 --> 08:56.280
Anything I can get.

08:56.340 --> 08:58.750
Keep my eyes and ears open.

08:58.780 --> 09:03.680
When the moment comes,
make a break for it.

09:03.720 --> 09:07.920
Before I can do that, though...

09:07.960 --> 09:09.260
I have to keep
my emotions in check.

09:10.860 --> 09:13.930
Give myself a chance
to recuperate.

09:20.860 --> 09:22.230
[Gunshot]

09:23.200 --> 09:27.200
Titan spotted at three o'clock!
Use the flare!

09:27.240 --> 09:29.900
We've got a smoke shell
fired from the right wing!

09:29.940 --> 09:32.040
We stay the course!
Tell the right wing

09:32.080 --> 09:34.910
to merge with the center
and maintain direction!

09:34.940 --> 09:36.840
The shortest path
is our only option.

09:36.910 --> 09:39.810
Straight ahead.
We have until sundown!

09:42.620 --> 09:48.090
[HANNES]
Mikasa. Hey, Mikasa. Hello?

09:48.120 --> 09:50.160
Stop pushing so hard.

09:50.230 --> 09:52.430
You're drifting up
into the vanguard.

09:52.460 --> 09:55.230
You wanna break
the whole formation?

09:55.270 --> 09:58.230
Look, I know how you feel.
But what'd I tell ya?

09:58.270 --> 09:59.930
Eren's not gonna
let those assholes

09:59.970 --> 10:01.900
get the best of him
without a fight.

10:01.940 --> 10:03.600
Agreed?

10:03.640 --> 10:05.640
[MIKASA]
Mm.

10:05.680 --> 10:07.940
Kid just doesn't
have it in him to give up.

10:07.980 --> 10:09.980
All we gotta do
is have a little faith.

10:10.010 --> 10:12.750
He'll hold his own
till the rest of us get there.

10:16.250 --> 10:18.720
Always has, always will.

10:40.280 --> 10:44.780
[YMIR sighs]
Hey, Reiner. Got any water?

10:44.810 --> 10:48.350
Help a girl out.
I'm dying over here.

10:48.380 --> 10:51.020
[REINER] Sorry, there's not
a helluva a lot I can do.

10:51.050 --> 10:54.720
Even if it is a matter
of life and death.

10:54.790 --> 10:57.160
That's comforting.
Well, at least now we know

10:57.190 --> 11:00.260
where we stand. Sort of.

11:02.000 --> 11:03.930
[REINER] Speaking of which.
We've been working

11:03.970 --> 11:09.470
our assess off. No food,
no sleep, no nothing.

11:09.510 --> 11:11.540
Ever since
those Titans showed up.

11:11.570 --> 11:13.440
That was yesterday, right?

11:13.510 --> 11:17.480
Man, we're lucky the wall
hasn't been destroyed.

11:17.510 --> 11:20.550
Still, you'd think that means
they'd give us a break.

11:20.580 --> 11:24.390
And don't even get me
started on promotion.

11:24.420 --> 11:26.890
What the hell?

11:26.920 --> 11:28.890
What? Aww, come on.

11:28.930 --> 11:31.760
I don't think that's
too much to ask, do you?

11:31.830 --> 11:34.230
God knows we've done
our share of heavy lifting

11:34.330 --> 11:36.660
all things considered.

11:36.700 --> 11:40.940
I mean, I get it,
we're soldiers. Duty first.

11:41.000 --> 11:44.540
It's just nice
to be acknowledged.

11:49.710 --> 11:51.780
You bang your head
or something?

11:51.850 --> 11:54.720
What're you even
talking about. Seriously?

11:54.750 --> 11:56.580
Ugh. Don't give me that.

11:56.620 --> 11:58.090
I'm not sayin' we
storm in and demand

11:58.120 --> 12:00.390
the rank of captain
or anything.

12:00.420 --> 12:02.890
[YMIR]
No. That's not what I mean.

12:02.930 --> 12:07.060
[REINER] Oh, yeah. Where'd you
find that cannon, by the way?

12:07.100 --> 12:10.030
I owe you one
for saving my bacon.

12:10.070 --> 12:11.800
[YMIR exhales]

12:11.870 --> 12:14.740
[REINER] Really nice of Christa
to patch me up afterwards.

12:14.770 --> 12:17.440
I'm starting to think me
and her might become a thing.

12:17.470 --> 12:18.610
[EREN]
Hey.

12:18.640 --> 12:20.370
Right? It's not just me?

12:20.410 --> 12:21.780
She always treats me
like we're--

12:21.810 --> 12:23.710
[EREN]
Hey!

12:26.950 --> 12:32.790
What's wrong with you?
You've got to be kidding me.

12:32.820 --> 12:36.260
Huh? What're you so
pissed about all of a sudden?

12:36.290 --> 12:39.130
Take it easy, man. Was it
something I said, or?

12:39.200 --> 12:42.060
If you wanna die,
then just keep talking!

12:42.100 --> 12:44.100
[YMIR]
Hold up, Eren.

12:44.130 --> 12:46.930
I think somebody's
gone off the deep end.

12:46.970 --> 12:50.740
Is that what this is, Bertholdt?

12:50.770 --> 12:52.570
If you know something we don't,

12:52.610 --> 12:55.610
now would be a good time
to put it on the table.

12:55.650 --> 12:57.250
Huh?

12:59.520 --> 13:02.950
[BERTHOLDT]
Reiner. Snap out of it.

13:02.990 --> 13:05.920
You're not a soldier, okay?

13:05.990 --> 13:10.420
You and I are... We're warriors.

13:10.460 --> 13:20.330
[REINER breathe quaveringly]

13:20.370 --> 13:23.100
[MARCO]
Reiner! What are you doing?

13:24.010 --> 13:28.640
[MARCO screams and gasps]

13:28.680 --> 13:31.210
[REINER]
Hey. Why...?

13:31.280 --> 13:33.880
[BERTHOLDT gasps]

13:33.950 --> 13:39.190
Why is Marco... being devoured?

13:46.530 --> 13:52.170
Right. I see.
That's how things are.

13:52.200 --> 13:57.240
[sobs softly]

14:00.180 --> 14:03.210
What the hell's he doing?

14:03.250 --> 14:07.650
I have a pretty good idea.
At least I think so.

14:07.680 --> 14:09.520
Didn't add up at first.

14:09.550 --> 14:11.420
Why would the man
who broke the wall

14:11.490 --> 14:14.590
risk his neck to save Conny?

14:14.660 --> 14:17.160
It's like the poor
bastard's personality is

14:17.190 --> 14:18.890
compartmentalized.

14:18.930 --> 14:22.000
Everything he does is
a contradiction in terms.

14:22.030 --> 14:23.660
He can't help it.

14:23.700 --> 14:25.500
On one hand,
he's a warrior bent on

14:25.540 --> 14:27.540
pushing mankind past the brink.

14:27.570 --> 14:30.270
On the other he's
pretending to be a solider.

14:30.340 --> 14:34.610
I'm thinking maybe he got
a little lost in the role.

14:34.680 --> 14:38.250
See. He can't resolve
those facets of himself.

14:38.280 --> 14:40.450
Can't bear the weight
of what he's done.

14:40.520 --> 14:42.480
The only way for him
to manage his conscience

14:42.520 --> 14:45.250
is to fall for his own act.

14:45.290 --> 14:48.420
He thinks he is a soldier.

14:48.460 --> 14:51.430
This is what you call
a split personality.

14:51.460 --> 14:53.130
He's gone insane.

14:53.200 --> 14:55.360
His heart and mind
are at war with each other,

14:55.400 --> 14:57.670
and judging by
Bertholdt's expression,

14:57.730 --> 15:01.200
this isn't the first stalemate.

15:01.240 --> 15:02.940
Blows me away!

15:02.970 --> 15:05.740
Wow, someone as brutally honest
as you losing their grip--

15:05.780 --> 15:11.750
[REINER]
Shut up! Not another word.

15:13.550 --> 15:17.890
I'm sorry.
Must've really hit a nerve.

15:21.390 --> 15:24.790
[EREN]
Is this some kind of joke?

15:24.830 --> 15:27.900
Where do you get off
pretending to be the victim?

15:27.960 --> 15:30.730
You're wallowing in self-pity?

15:30.770 --> 15:34.270
How dare you. What was
going through your head

15:34.300 --> 15:37.170
the day I told you
my story, huh?

15:37.240 --> 15:39.610
Remember that, Bertholdt?

15:39.640 --> 15:42.680
I'm talking to you, lackey!

15:42.750 --> 15:44.910
I told you everything.

15:44.950 --> 15:47.620
You sat there and looked me
straight in the eye.

15:47.650 --> 15:50.580
Watched me relive seeing
my mother eaten alive.

15:50.620 --> 15:53.990
[EREN]
Stop it! No!

15:54.020 --> 15:55.690
Don't you remember?

15:55.760 --> 15:57.590
Well, it just so happens
the chunk of wall

15:57.630 --> 15:59.690
you kicked out
fell on our house.

15:59.760 --> 16:03.200
It's what kept her from
being able to run away.

16:03.270 --> 16:07.970
Ring any bells? Take you back?

16:08.000 --> 16:10.300
Let me ask you again.

16:10.340 --> 16:15.780
What was going through your head
when I told you that story?

16:18.210 --> 16:21.650
Want me to be honest?

16:21.680 --> 16:25.950
In the moment I felt...
sorry for you.

16:30.190 --> 16:35.560
[EREN]
Huh. Sorry for me?

16:35.630 --> 16:39.400
So, then. You're not...

16:39.470 --> 16:45.710
You're not warriors or soldiers.
You're just murderers.

16:45.740 --> 16:48.310
Psychotic mass-murderers
who snuffed out the lives

16:48.340 --> 16:50.640
of countless people that
never did you any wrong.

16:50.680 --> 16:52.510
Don't you think
I'm aware of that fact?

16:52.550 --> 16:55.020
I don't need you shoving it
down my goddamn throat!

16:55.050 --> 16:56.820
Then stop acting
like you've got any right

16:56.850 --> 16:58.590
to feel sorry for yourself!

16:58.650 --> 17:01.090
We're living in a hell
you two created!

17:01.160 --> 17:02.560
Are you proud of yourselves?

17:02.590 --> 17:04.330
You're not one of us!
You've never been!

17:04.390 --> 17:06.430
You're not even human anymore!

17:06.500 --> 17:07.900
[REINER]
You want an apology?

17:07.960 --> 17:09.930
Is that what you hope to get
out of calling us murderers?

17:10.000 --> 17:12.700
Want us to feel bad?
Want us to take the blame?

17:12.740 --> 17:14.540
Who are you talking to?

17:14.570 --> 17:16.400
The people you thought
you knew don't exist!

17:16.440 --> 17:19.410
They're dead! But hey,
if screaming does it for ya,

17:19.440 --> 17:23.040
go ahead and scream
your goddamn head off!

17:26.250 --> 17:35.560
[REINER panting]

17:35.590 --> 17:37.960
[EREN]
You're right.

17:38.030 --> 17:43.860
Who am I? What do I know?

17:43.900 --> 17:50.770
Still. I've got to do
something. Anything.

17:50.870 --> 17:53.270
I swear to you,
one way or another,

17:53.310 --> 17:58.450
the two of you will pay.
And it's gonna hurt.

18:05.820 --> 18:08.260
[YMIR]
You can't be for real.

18:08.290 --> 18:09.790
Huh?

18:09.830 --> 18:12.290
Eren, grow up.
Keep spouting off

18:12.330 --> 18:15.930
childish bullshit like that
and I've got no hope for you.

18:15.970 --> 18:18.070
[EREN grunts]

18:20.740 --> 18:22.540
[YMIR]
Tell me something.

18:24.910 --> 18:27.240
What's with the giant monkey?

18:30.410 --> 18:33.080
[REINER] Monkey?
What're you talking about?

18:33.120 --> 18:36.150
Huh. I thought
for sure you'd know.

18:36.190 --> 18:39.190
That's surprising. From the way
you guys were ogling it

18:39.260 --> 18:41.020
all slack-jawed
I figured we were seeing

18:41.090 --> 18:43.290
some kind of living legend.

18:43.330 --> 18:45.330
Weird.

18:45.360 --> 18:48.360
A monkey? Don't be cute.

18:48.430 --> 18:52.030
Shut up and listen.
Monkey, Beast Titan.

18:52.100 --> 18:56.100
Whatever you wanna call him,
he's behind this latest fiasco.

18:56.140 --> 18:59.440
It's why Titans are
cropping up out of nowhere.

18:59.480 --> 19:04.040
I get the feeling
he's gauging our strength.

19:04.110 --> 19:07.310
Reiner and Betholdt are
trying to get wherever he is.

19:07.350 --> 19:09.380
It's how they're
getting back home.

19:09.450 --> 19:12.050
Feel free to correct me
if I'm way off base.

19:12.120 --> 19:13.190
[Gasps]

19:13.220 --> 19:16.720
Wait. How did you know?
Who are you?

19:16.790 --> 19:18.360
What else haven't you told me?

19:18.390 --> 19:21.730
Be patient. I'm caught up
in circumstances of my own.

19:21.800 --> 19:24.530
What the hell is that
supposed to mean?

19:24.570 --> 19:26.900
Eren. If you think
killing these morons

19:26.970 --> 19:30.840
will put an end to all of this,
you are sorely mistaken.

19:30.870 --> 19:33.640
[EREN]
Huh? But then who's the enemy?

19:33.680 --> 19:35.040
The enemy?

19:35.080 --> 19:36.810
Look, if I told you,
things would get too--

19:36.850 --> 19:41.080
[REINER] Ymir! There's no future
for this world and you know it.

19:41.150 --> 19:42.380
[YMIR gasps]

19:42.490 --> 19:44.050
[REINER] You have
a solid grasp of things.

19:44.090 --> 19:45.820
What d'you think comes next?

19:45.860 --> 19:47.920
Joining our side wouldn't
be out of the question

19:47.990 --> 19:50.060
if you were so inclined.

19:50.090 --> 19:53.030
[YMIR] And put my faith
in you guys? That's rich.

19:53.060 --> 19:55.700
Neither of you trusts me
as far as you can throw me.

19:55.730 --> 19:58.570
[REINER]
Come on. That isn't true.

19:58.670 --> 20:01.240
We know what you really want.

20:01.270 --> 20:04.070
All you care about
is protecting Christa.

20:05.940 --> 20:10.040
If we can all agree on that,
I don't see the conflict.

20:10.080 --> 20:12.580
I'm being absolutely serious.

20:12.620 --> 20:16.020
Is it so hard to believe we
want what's best for her, too?

20:16.050 --> 20:18.920
Hate to break it to ya,
but you're not the only one.

20:18.950 --> 20:22.020
Then again, you could always
put your trust in Eren,

20:22.060 --> 20:24.190
see where that leads you.

20:24.230 --> 20:25.730
What?

20:28.700 --> 20:31.070
[REINER] You're probably
leaning toward escape.

20:31.100 --> 20:34.570
Better to take a chance with him
than throw in with us, right?

20:34.600 --> 20:36.440
Because if we
end up taking you,

20:36.470 --> 20:39.640
there's not much hope
of being rescued.

20:39.710 --> 20:42.610
I'll be straight with you.
That much is true.

20:42.650 --> 20:44.910
Even if you came willingly,
we're not in a position

20:44.950 --> 20:47.550
to guarantee your safety.

20:47.580 --> 20:49.880
But if it's Christa
we're talking about,

20:49.920 --> 20:51.450
we might be able
to do something.

20:51.490 --> 20:54.890
[YMIR Gasps and snarls]

20:54.920 --> 20:57.290
[REINER] It's your call.
What's it gonna be?

20:57.330 --> 21:03.160
Is it Christa's future?
Or your own petty existence?

21:03.230 --> 21:05.930
[EREN] Is there really
no future for this world?

21:05.970 --> 21:08.570
Why? And the monkey.

21:08.600 --> 21:11.440
How does he figure into this?

21:11.470 --> 21:14.780
Come clean!
Who's the real enemy?

21:14.810 --> 21:18.080
Tell me what you know!

21:18.110 --> 21:20.450
Who is it?!

21:22.850 --> 21:26.850
[YMIR sighs]

21:26.920 --> 21:28.320
Couldn't say.

21:28.360 --> 21:29.660
[EREN grunts]

21:29.690 --> 21:33.490
[REINER]
All right, then. Sorry, Eren.

21:35.000 --> 21:37.660
[Distant gunshot]

21:43.870 --> 21:47.780
[BERTHOLDT]
The Scouts are here? Already?

21:47.810 --> 21:50.840
[REINER grunts]
Son of a bitch!

21:50.950 --> 21:55.550
[EREN]
No. Damn you, Ymir!

21:57.990 --> 22:01.820
[EREN] Only one hour
left until sunset.

22:09.930 --> 22:14.940
♪ Closing Song
